</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"1">When Francis pitched the clean "30/20/20/30"=
 split, he was speaking in <i data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-index-in-node=3D=
"71">Pre-Money</i> conceptual shorthand. He is talking about how to divide =
the initial 10,000,000 authorized shares <i data-path-to-node=3D"1" data-in=
dex-in-node=3D"178">before</i> the investors' money converts.</p><p data-pa=
th-to-node=3D"2">However, investors using Post-Money SAFEs do not take thei=
r shares out of a pre-existing "sleeve" of the 10M pool. Instead, their own=
ership is mathematically locked by their investment amount and their valuat=
ion cap (e.g., $500k investment at a $4M Cap =3D exactly 12.5% of the compa=
ny).</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"3">To give them that guaranteed 12.5%, the =
total number of shares must expand (as you correctly modeled in your 12.3M =
total), which means everyone in the initial 10M pool gets diluted proportio=
nally.</p><h3 data-path-to-node=3D"4">The Reality of Francis's Math</h3><p =
data-path-to-node=3D"5">Let's look at the actual Fully Diluted percentages =
of the model you just drafted. (Note: the percentages for the base shares d=
rop significantly once the 12.3M fully diluted total is calculated).</p><ul=
